{"id": "unknown-2026-11-10-012", "date": "2026-11-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Case study: Yousee Display uses flexible AMOLED and \"Zero-Dead-Angle\" 3D curved bonding to create expressive robot faces", "content": "<p>Humanoid robots are quickly moving from research labs into hotels, shopping malls, classrooms and homes, and a robot's face is fast becoming its most important interface. A display built into the face can show digital eyes, expressions, greetings and operating status, which turns a machine into something people naturally want to interact with. Wrapping a display around a curved robot head is far from simple, though. Imprecise 3D fitting, inconsistent image quality and weak surface protection ", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/case-study-yousee-display-uses-flexible-amoled-and-zero-dead-angle-3d-curved", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-10-013", "date": "2026-11-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Cyan is emerging as a signal for autonomous driving: UDC, OLEDWorks and Audi to evaluate light-blue OLED lighting", "content": "<p><a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/universal-display\">Universal Display</a> (UDC) and <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/oledworks\">OLEDWorks</a> announced a collaboration to evaluate cyan OLED lighting for automated driving system (ADS) communication. The two companies will combine UDC's phosphorescent blue OLED materials with OLEDWorks' OLED panel development and production expertise, and Audi is also taking part in the evaluation.</p><a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/files/m", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/universal-display-and-oledworks-evaluate-cyan-oled-lighting-automated-driving", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-10-014", "date": "2026-11-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["mass production", "delay"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "HKC's 6-Gen OLED fab in Mianyang falls behind schedule, no major equipment has been ordered yet", "content": "<p>China's <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/hkc\">HKC</a> is reportedly falling behind schedule with its plan to build a 6-Gen OLED production line (H7) in Mianyang, Sichuan Province. HKC originally aimed to install deposition equipment in March 2027 and to start mass production in June 2028, but according to industry sources it has not yet ordered any of the line's major equipment.</p><a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/files/mcp-uploads/HKC-H7-6Gen-OLED-delay.png\" target=\"_blank\"", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/hkcs-6-gen-oled-fab-mianyang-falls-behind-schedule-no-major-equipment-has-been", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-11-10-015", "date": "2026-11-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Samsung Display earns automotive cybersecurity certifications for its automotive OLED displays", "content": "<p><a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/samsung-oled\">Samsung Display</a> announced that it has earned two automotive cybersecurity certifications, ISO/SAE 21434 and ENX VCS. The company says that it is the first in the industry to receive both at the same time, and that the certifications will strengthen its automotive OLED business as carmakers move to software-defined vehicles (SDVs), in which cybersecurity has become a critical requirement.</p><a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/f", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/samsung-display-earns-isosae-21434-and-enx-vcs-automotive-cybersecurity", "type": "rss"}]}
